    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <pb n="1" facs="Edgeworth_Geneve_1816-03-08_page01.jpg"/>
                
                <opener>
                    <dateline> 
                        <note>33</note>
                        <date when="1816-03-08" cert="high"> <unclear>8</unclear> March 16 </date>
                        <placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#Edgeworthstown_IE">Edgeworthstown</placeName> 
                        <placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#IE">Ireland</placeName>
                        </dateline> </opener>
                
                 <p>
                  The best return I can make<lb/>
                  for your uncommon<lb/>
                  goodness and for the valuable<lb/>
                  sacrifice of your time is<lb/>
                  to shew you that we have<lb/>
                  profited by your kindness.<lb/></p>
                  <p>
                  I do not mean to<lb/>
                  encroach upon you so far<lb/>
                  as to ask you to send the<lb/>
                  enclosed; I only beg that you<lb/>
                  will cast your eye over it<lb/>
                  &amp; send it to <persName ref="./Personography.xml#JohnJ1">Johnson</persName> &amp; Co.<lb/></p>
                  <p>
                  I have expunged the<lb/>
                  passage relative to clerical<lb/>
                  Tutors<lb/>
                      
                  <pb n="2" facs="Edgeworth_Geneve_1816-03-08_page02.jpg"/>
                  though I thought it had been<lb/>
                  sufficiently guarded against<lb/>
                  all blame of encouraging<lb/>
                  Sycophants - In the<lb/>
                  rest of the chapter I had<lb/>
                  good reasons as a member<lb/>
                  of the Board of Education<lb/>
                  to be careful - I have done<lb/>
                  some good &amp; hope to do<lb/>
                  more at that Board by the<lb/>
                  assistance of the <persName ref="./Personography.xml#StuaW1" cert="high">Arch<hi rend="superscript">p</hi>.</persName> of<lb/>
                  <del><placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#Armagh_IE">Armagh</placeName></del> <placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#Armagh_IE">Armagh</placeName> - We shall<lb/>
                  leave out <persName ref="./Personography.xml#WattI1">Watts</persName> though his<lb/>
                  <title ref="./Workography.xml#Impro1">Improvement of the mind</title><lb/>
                  is a good book -<lb/></p>
                  <p>
                  <persName ref="./Personography.xml#LockJ2">Locke</persName> was in high favor at<lb/>
                  <placeName ref="./Placeography.xml#Oxford_ENK">Oxford</placeName> when I was there<lb/></p>
                  <p>
                  May I use your remarks<lb/>
                  on <persName ref="./Personography.xml#PascB1">Pascal</persName> <del>&amp;</del> <persName ref="./Personography.xml#BossJ1">Bossuet</persName> &amp; <persName ref="./Personography.xml#MassJ1">Massillon.</persName><lb/>
                
                  <pb n="3" facs="Edgeworth_Geneve_1816-03-08_page03.jpg"/>
                  <note>34</note>3
                  - So I however do not pretend<lb/>
                  in this Essay to teach Theology.<lb/></p>
                  <p>
                  What <persName ref="./Personography.xml#RomiS1">Sir S Romilly</persName> says<lb/>
                  about encouraging boys <choice><orig>intend<lb/>
                  ed</orig><reg>intended</reg></choice> for the law to be strenuous<lb/>
                  in argument I think perfectly<lb/>
                  just - It was mentioned rather<lb/>
                  playfully - but it is expunged<lb/>
                  - as every thing shall be<lb/>
                  from my writings that<lb/>
                  countenances art<del>s</del> instead<lb/>
                  of truth.<lb/></p>
                  <closer>
                  Your obliged<lb/>
                  <persName ref="./Personography.xml#EdgeR1">Rich<hi rend="superscript">d</hi> Lovell Edgeworth</persName><lb/></closer>
                
                 <pb n="4" facs="Edgeworth_Geneve_1816-03-08_page04.jpg"/>
                  <closer><address>
                  <addrLine><unclear>M<hi rend="superscript">r</hi></unclear> <persName ref="./Personography.xml#DumoE1">Dumont Esq</persName></addrLine>
                  <addrLine>&amp;c &amp;c &amp;c</addrLine></address>
                  </closer>
             
                
                
